(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// The RTS's semantics of GHC's non-threaded runtime (HE4e; doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md, \"As built: HE4d,"] [10 1 "// HE4e (write-ahead)\"): throwTo blocking its thrower while the target masks (HES41 (a), rts/RaiseAsync.c's throwTo and"] [11 1 "// maybePerformBlockedException), the reachability GHC's collector decides (rts/sm/MarkWeak.c): blocked threads no root"] [12 1 "// reaches resurrected with BlockedIndefinitelyOnMVar, OnSTM or NonTermination (Schedule.c's resurrectThreads), weak"] [13 1 "// pointers whose keys no root reaches finalized (Weak.c's scheduleFinalizers: the C finalizers at once, the Haskell ones"] [14 1 "// by a thread running runFinalizerBatch), at performGC and when every thread is blocked; and the delimited"] [15 1 "// continuations of prompt# and control0# (rts/Continuation.c)."] [17 1 "// throwMsg is a throwTo# waiting for its target to accept it (GHC's MessageThrowTo): queued on the target, its thrower"] [18 1 "// blocked on it."] [26 1 "// ---- throwTo ----"] [28 1 "// accepts reports whether t takes an asynchronous exception now (RaiseAsync.c's throwToMsg by t's state)."] [34 22 "// a blackhole is not interruptible"] [36 2 "// an MVar, a delay, STM, a throwTo of its own: interruptible"] [40 1 "// throwTo raises x in t if t accepts it now (true), else queues it on t for src, which must block (false). A finished"] [41 1 "// target takes it as delivered."] [55 1 "// raiseIn raises x in t at once, whatever its masking state (GHC's throwToSingleThreaded): t taken off what it"] [56 1 "// waits on and made runnable at the handler (or ended)."] [61 29 "// a runnable thread is in the run queue already (review 189, L7)"] [76 1 "// pendingFor is t's first queued exception it accepts in its state now (maybePerformBlockedException's test), or nil."] [92 1 "// deliverSelf raises the current thread's first acceptable queued exception (at an unmasking, or as it blocks"] [93 1 "// interruptibly while masked interruptibly), its thrower woken; ok false when there is none."] [107 1 "// throwDone wakes a delivered exception's thrower: its throwTo# returns."] [116 1 "// finished wakes the throwers queued on a thread that ended (awakenBlockedExceptionQueue)."] [126 1 "// killThread is killThread# (throwTo): to itself raised at once; to another thread raised when it accepts it, else"] [127 1 "// the thrower blocks, interruptibly, until it does."] [140 1 "// ---- reachability ----"] [142 1 "// gcInfo is what a frame of code keeps alive: the slots its continuation reads and the globals its code names."] [322 1 "// gc decides what GHC's major collection would (MarkWeak.c's stages): the roots (the running and runnable threads,"] [323 1 "// the sleeping ones, the stable pointers) marked, the weak pointers whose keys are marked keeping their values and"] [324 1 "// finalizers, then the blocked threads still unmarked resurrected (marked: what they reach lives), the weak pointers"] [325 1 "// again, the rest dead. The dead weak pointers are finalized; the resurrected threads, oldest first, get their"] [326 1 "// exceptions. It returns the number of threads resurrected."] [383 2 "// the dead weak pointers, oldest first"] [408 4 "// a thread blocked in throwTo: its target wakes and carries on (resurrectThreads)"] [420 1 "// alive reports a weak pointer's key reachable (a key that is no heap object always is)."] [432 1 "// finalize finalizes dead weak pointers (Weak.c's scheduleFinalizers): each marked dead, its C finalizers run (the"] [433 1 "// last added first), the Haskell finalizers given to one new thread running runFinalizerBatch (which runs the last"] [434 1 "// first: the newest weak pointer's first)."] [457 1 "// runCFins runs a weak pointer's C finalizers, the last added first (runCFinalizers)."] [466 5 "// a finalizer of the program's own C (cprog.go)"] [484 1 "// exitCFins runs the C finalizers of every weak pointer still alive (hs_exit's runAllCFinalizers)."] [493 1 "// lambdaGC is what a closure's code names (its body's and its nested closures' globals), its code compiled first."] [498 19 "// a cycle through the code: its own globals are being collected"] [515 1 "// caseGC is what a case's frame keeps alive: the slots its alternatives read (less those they bind) and the globals"] [516 1 "// they name."] [544 1 "// exprGC is the globals a thread's next expression names."] [639 5 "// the nested closure's code: its globals (its slots are its own frame's)"] [650 1 "// ---- delimited continuations ----"] [652 1 "// Cont is a continuation control0# captured: the frames above its prompt, their slots copied, and the masking state"] [653 1 "// to restore when it resumes (when the frames hold a mask frame: Continuation.c's apply_mask_frame, outer the index"] [654 1 "// of the outermost)."] [662 1 "// contLam is a continuation's code as a function of two arguments (the IO action resumed with, the state token)."] [667 1 "// copyFrames is a copy of frames whose case frames' slots are copies too (a frame sharing slots with another shares"] [668 1 "// the copy)."] [698 3 "// the outermost mask frame now restores the resuming context's state; the captured state applies inside"] [749 3 "// abort to the prompt: the frames and the prompt popped, the masking state the prompt's"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[110 17] [372 36] [461 22] [461 30] [465 28] [495 24] [518 26] [704 35] [725 7] [725 15] [762 37]]} (go/file "rts.go" :imports [


